Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.9.2-0

%labels
    Application ServerQwen GPU pipeline environment
    Pipeline Qwen3.5-9B variant analysis (vLLM)

%files
    environment.yml /opt/environment.yml

%post
    set -eu
    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends curl ca-certificates
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # Single source of truth for the pipeline's Python deps is the repo-root
    # environment.yml (also used by the native install and the Dockerfile)
    # — built here instead of re-pinned,
    # so updating that one file is enough to rebuild an in-sync image; no
    # separate lockfile to drift out of sync with it.
    conda env create -f /opt/environment.yml -n env-vllm-pipeline
    conda clean -afy

%environment
    export PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export PATH=/opt/conda/envs/env-vllm-pipeline/bin:$PATH

%runscript
    exec "$@"

%help
    ServerQwen GPU-side runtime environment: Python 3.11 + vLLM + the CUDA
    stack vLLM's own wheels bring (nvcc/cudnn/nccl/cutlass — no host CUDA
    module needed) + the pipeline's Python dependencies, built from
    environment.yml.

    This image is the RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT ONLY. Neither the pipeline code
    nor the model weights are baked in — both are fetched/mounted at run
    time, so this .sif stays small (image is ~7.6GB of Python/CUDA packages
    only) and works for any model or code revision without a rebuild:

      - Pipeline code (Qwen_Engine_IVA/IVA_vllm/, prompts/)
        — bind-mount the repo at run time:
            apptainer exec --nv --bind /work/PRTNR/...:/work/PRTNR/... \
                iva-gpu.sif vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B --dtype bfloat16 ...

      - Model weights (Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B, ~18GB) — downloaded by vLLM from
        the Hugging Face Hub on first run via the huggingface_hub client
        library baked into this image; the weights themselves are never
        part of the build. Apptainer bind-mounts the real $HOME by default,
        so the download lands in $HOME/.cache/huggingface and is reused on
        every subsequent run — no re-download per job. On Curnagl, point
        HF_HOME at shared project storage instead of $HOME (quota) before
        the first run, e.g.:
            export HF_HOME=/work/PRTNR/.../ServerQwen/.hf_cache
        Pre-warm the cache once via `huggingface-cli download Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B`
        (inside the container) if you want the first `vllm serve` on a GPU
        node to skip the download entirely.

    Build (on a node with internet access, e.g. login node):
        apptainer build iva-gpu.sif iva-gpu.def

    Run vLLM on a GPU node (--nv maps the host NVIDIA driver in):
        apptainer exec --nv iva-gpu.sif \
            vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B --dtype bfloat16 \
            --max-model-len 32768 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \
            --port 38103 --enable-prefix-caching

    Run the pipeline's own FastAPI server (direct mode) the same way, from
    inside Qwen_Engine_IVA/IVA_vllm/:
        apptainer exec --nv iva-gpu.sif \
            uvicorn server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
